{"strongs": "H0188", "word": "אוֺי", "translit": "oy", "root": "אוה", "morph": "H:Intj", "pos": "interjection", "gloss": "woe!", "definition": "אוֺי interjection (onomatopoetic; compare , ) woe! an impassioned expression of grief and despair: usually with dative אוֺי לִי Isa 6:5 woe to me! for I am undone, so Isa 24:16 ; Jer 10:19 ; Jer 15:10 אוֺי לָנוּ woe to us! 1Sam 4:7 ; 1Sam 4:8 ; Jer 4:13 ; Jer 6:4 אוֺינָֿא לִי Jer 4:31 ; Jer 45:3 אוֺינָֿא לָנוּ Lam 5:16 . With the 2nd or 3rd person often implying a denunciation; אוֺילְֿךָ מוֺאָב Num 21:29 (= Jer 48:46 ) Jer 13:27 ; Ezek 16:23 repeated אוֺי אוֺי לָח ; Isa 3:9 אוֺי לְנַפְשָׁם v Isa 3:11 ; Hos 7:13 ; Hos 9:12 (|| שֹׁד לָהֶם ). With a voc. (or implicit accusative) Ezek 24:6 ; Ezek 24:9 אוֺי עִיר הַדָּמִים ; absolute Num 24:23 . Used as a substantive Prov 23:29 לְמִי אוֺי (|| לְמִי אֲבוֺי ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB185')\">BDB185</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H188')\">H188</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB184')\">BDB184</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB186')\">BDB186</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אוֺי</bdbheb> <b>interjection</b> (onomatopoetic; compare <placeholder87/>, <placeholder88/>) <highlightword>woe!</highlightword> an impassioned expression of grief and despair: usually with dative <bdbheb>אוֺי לִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 6:5\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(23,6,5)\">Isa 6:5</ref> <highlight>woe</highlight> to me! for I am undone, so <ref ref=\"Isa 24:16\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(23,24,16)\">Isa 24:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 10:19\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(24,10,19)\">Jer 10:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 15:10\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(24,15,10)\">Jer 15:10</ref> <bdbheb>אוֺי לָנוּ</bdbheb> <highlight>woe</highlight> to us! <ref ref=\"1Sam 4:7\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(9,4,7)\">1Sam 4:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 4:8\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(9,4,8)\">1Sam 4:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 4:13\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(24,4,13)\">Jer 4:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 6:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,6,4)\">Jer 6:4</ref> <bdbheb>אוֺינָֿא לִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 4:31\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(24,4,31)\">Jer 4:31</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 45:3\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(24,45,3)\">Jer 45:3</ref> <bdbheb>אוֺינָֿא לָנוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lam 5:16\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(25,5,16)\">Lam 5:16</ref>. With the 2nd or 3rd person often implying a denunciation; <bdbheb>אוֺילְֿךָ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>מוֺאָב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 21:29\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(4,21,29)\">Num 21:29</ref> (= <ref ref=\"Jer 48:46\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"46\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"46\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,46)\">Jer 48:46</ref>) <ref ref=\"Jer 13:27\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,27)\">Jer 13:27</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 16:23\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,23)\">Ezek 16:23</ref> repeated <bdbheb>אוֺי אוֺי לָח</bdbheb>; <ref ref=\"Isa 3:9\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(23,3,9)\">Isa 3:9</ref> <bdbheb>אוֺי לְנַפְשָׁם</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Isa 3:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,3,11)\">Isa 3:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 7:13\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(28,7,13)\">Hos 7:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 9:12\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(28,9,12)\">Hos 9:12</ref> (|| <bdbheb>שֹׁד לָהֶם</bdbheb>). With a voc. (or implicit accusative) <ref ref=\"Ezek 24:6\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(26,24,6)\">Ezek 24:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 24:9\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(26,24,9)\">Ezek 24:9</ref> <bdbheb>אוֺי עִיר הַדָּמִים</bdbheb>; absolute <ref ref=\"Num 24:23\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(4,24,23)\">Num 24:23</ref>. Used as a substantive <ref ref=\"Prov 23:29\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(20,23,29)\">Prov 23:29</ref> <bdbheb>לְמִי אוֺי</bdbheb> (|| <bdbheb>לְמִי אֲבוֺי</bdbheb>). </p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Isa 6:5", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 6, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Isa 24:16", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 24, "verse": 16}, {"raw": "Jer 10:19", "book": "JER", "chapter": 10, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "Jer 15:10", "book": "JER", "chapter": 15, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "1Sam 4:7", "book": "1SA", "chapter": 4, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "1Sam 4:8", "book": "1SA", "chapter": 4, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Jer 4:13", "book": "JER", "chapter": 4, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Jer 6:4", "book": "JER", "chapter": 6, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Jer 4:31", "book": "JER", "chapter": 4, "verse": 31}, {"raw": "Jer 45:3", "book": "JER", "chapter": 45, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Lam 5:16", "book": "LAM", "chapter": 5, "verse": 16}, {"raw": "Num 21:29", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 21, "verse": 29}, {"raw": "Jer 48:46", "book": "JER", "chapter": 48, "verse": 46}, {"raw": "Jer 13:27", "book": "JER", "chapter": 13, "verse": 27}, {"raw": "Ezek 16:23", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 16, "verse": 23}, {"raw": "Isa 3:9", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 3, "verse": 9}, {"raw": "Isa 3:11", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 3, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Hos 7:13", "book": "HOS", "chapter": 7, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Hos 9:12", "book": "HOS", "chapter": 9, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Ezek